he had suffered  a miscarriage  and if i'm being completely honest i  don't think her relationship status was  all of that much interest to karl  tanzler he couldn't care less as she was  separated in a loving marriage a widow  or one of those strange americans you  hear about who marries their car  he wanted her and he was going to have  her even if he did happen to be 32 years  her senior there was admittedly one of a  small problem with this plan  elena hadn't been admitted to hospital  for a run-of-the-mill checkup  she had tuberculosis which considering  the lack of an available cure in those  days was basically a death sentence even  today tb remains one of the world's  leading causes of death claiming 1.5  million lives in 2020.  carl was understandably devastated but  despite not really knowing all that much  about tb or you know actually being a  doctor he made it his life's mission to  save elena he immediately began  experimenting with various tonics and  concoctions in the hopes that he'd  stumble across a cure  with the permission of eleanor's family  carl began administering these  treatments in their home which was soon  full of various gadgets that he'd  managed to steal from the hospital  now so far karl tanzler might not sound  like all that much of a bad guy i mean  he was doing everything in his power to  try and save eleanor  even if some of his methods were a  little  unconventional  if he'd stopped there history probably  would have remembered him as a misguided  and medically irresponsible dreamer  rather than an utter psychopath  but  yeah he didn't stop there  not even close despite carl's best  efforts eleanor died in october 1931.  he was so devastated he offered to pay  for the funeral and for an expensive  mausoleum in key west cemetery  her family saw it as a kind gesture  but in reality it should have been a  massive red flag because little did they  know carl would keep hold of the  mausoleum's only key  and this is where our richard curtis  romcom  meets tim burton  for more than a year tonsler visited  eleanor's grave every single night  he would sit by her coffin  chatting away as though eleanor still  lived  if anything his death only seemed to  have increased his devotion  but then all of a sudden  the visit stopped  in hindsight that should have been  another red flag but i guess helena's  family simply assumed carl tunzler had  finally moved on  of course there was only one other  reason he would have stopped visiting  eleanor's grave  if she wasn't in it anymore  according to carl himself elena's spirit  had appeared to him and asked to be  taken back to his house  not one to take the words of the dead  lightly as we've already seen  one night in april 1933 carl removed  eleanor's body from its resting place  and brought it home with him  he'd been told he'd marry this woman and  he wasn't going to let a silly little  thing like death stand in his way  there were of course a few logistical  issues with carl's new relationship  status  elena had been dead for 18 months and  she was aging like a mr whippy in the  sahara in an effort to stem the decay  karl built a makeshift lab in his house  and then he got to work  he stabilized the body's shape with coat  hangers and wires and stuffed a torso  with rags to fill things out a little  he applied mortician's wax to the face  and fashioned a wig out of what remained  of her hair  he even replaced her eyes with glass  orbs  tonsler disinfected the body regularly  and that's along with liberal use of  strong perfumes  went some way towards masking his new  bride's unfortunate odor  by the time he was finished tonsler's  dream had finally come true and for the  first time in his life he was truly  happy with all the enthusiasm of a  newlywed he spent almost every moment of  every day with eleanor's corpse he sat  it at the dinner table whilst he ate  danced with it in the living room and  even laid the body beside him in bed as  he slept  hopefully  of course all his actions soon began to  produce inevitable signs of wear and  tear on tanzler's new wife  to make matters even worse what remained  of eleanor's body was slowly rotting  away to nothing  apparently dating an actual skeleton was  too much even for carl tanzler so he  replaced elena's skin with silk cloth  coated in wax and plaster of paris  essentially building himself a human  doll made from bits of real human  somehow this absolutely bat-shit insane  situation continued for about seven  years without anybody noticing  meaning eleanor had been dead for almost  nine years this is the part in our  classic rom-com where you walk out of  the cinema because it's disgusting  but it turns out carl didn't want things  to go on this way forever you see over  the years he'd been working on a  strategy to bring his wife back to life  for good  the plan basically involved building a  rocket and launching elena's dead body  into space  where he hoped radiation would restore  her to the land of the living  which admittedly was a tad ambitious  but hey  in the end carl never got to find out  whether this ingenious plan would have  worked  though i'm prepared to go out on a limb  here and say it probably wouldn't have  rumors were beginning to spread around  key west about that weird old man who  lived alone and hardly left his house  except to buy women's clothes and  suspiciously large quantities of perfume  one day a local boy passing the house  happened to see carl dancing with what  looked like a large doll in the living  room i suppose we can't really blame him  for not immediately suspecting carl was  living with a nine-year-old corpse but  anyway  others were growing suspicious too  particularly eleanor's sister florinda  who perhaps unsurprisingly had never  been carl's biggest fan  with his story now the talk of the town  florinda paid carl a visit in 1940 and  it's safe to say she was shocked by what  she found  the nine-year-old remained of her sister  in a dress  the authorities were immediately alerted  and carl was arrested  an autopsy soon uncovered the full  disturbing details of the horrific  makeover  including certain  modifications carl had made to  facilitate the consummation of his  marriage to eleanor  yeah this is the part in our classic  rom-com where it gets banned from  netflix for being too graphic  despite taking a dead body to his house  living with it  loving it and planning to shoot it into  space a psychiatric evaluation actually  deemed carl tanzler to be mentally  competent enough to stand trial  he faced the charges of maliciously  destroying a grave and removing the body  without authorization  but in perhaps the biggest shock of this  whole story the case against carl was  dropped  and he served not a single day of  present time  not because he wasn't very obviously  guilty but because the statute of  limitations had expired for his offence  as a result carl tunsler was free to go  and he even received quite a lot of  positive press coverage and public  support  as many people at the time saw his  actions as just plain old romantic  people were weird in the old days  in one final twist to this strange  gruesome story  poor old eleanor's body wasn't  reinterred after finally being rescued  from carl's clutches  but put on display at a funeral home  the story was big news and thousands of  people lined up to get a look at her  including carl tunzler himself rumor has  it he'd even asked the authorities if he  could have the body returned to him as  you can probably imagine the request was  denied after interest in the case died  down eleanor was finally laid to rest  once more  this time at a secret location just in  case carl got any ideas  [Music]  in later life tanzler received u.s  citizenship and wrote an autobiography  oh and do you remember doris  that wife he had before any of this  weirdness happened  you know the mother of his children that  he walked out on  well they remained friends  you'd think it would be awkward what  with him fancying a dead body more than  her and all that but apparently not  and she even supported him financially  in his later years  i'm sure carl was grateful but he never  gave up on his one true love  when he died in 1952 his body was found  with a life-sized doll  that bore a striking resemblance to his  corpse bride  it's been suggested by some that carl  somehow found out where the real eleanor  was buried and switched to body with a  fake  but there's no real evidence to support  that story and as the credits roll on  our awful rom-com i have to say it's  much more likely that it was indeed just  a doll  either way  carl tanzler's life is surely the  weirdest love story never told  and a useful reminder of how not to take  a girl out  [Music]  thanks for watching
 

